G4005.def:
πεντηκοστός, -ή, -όν 
[in LXX for חֲמִישִׁי, חֲמִישִׁי, Lévitique 25:10-11, 4Ki.15:23 15:27; 1Ma.4:1-61, 2Ma.14:4; ἡ π., Tob.2:1, 2Ma.12:32 * ;] 
fiftieth. As subst., ἡ π.; 
__(a) (sc. μερίς), at Athens, a tax of two per cent.; 
__(b) (sc. ἡμέρα, i.e. the fiftieth day after the Passover), Pentecost, the second of the three great Jewish feasts (To, 2Mac, ll. with; ἑορτὴ ἑβδομάδων, Deutéronome 16:10, al.) : Actes 2:1 20:16, 1 Corinthiens 16:8.†

G4008.def:
πέραν 
adv., [in LXX for עֵבֶר and cognate forms ;] 
on the other side, across (usually with the idea of water lying between); 
__(a) as in the older poets, as prep. with genitive: τ. θαλάσσης, Jean 6:1, 17 6:22, 25; τ. Ἰορδάνου, Matthieu 4:15 (LXX), Matthieu 4:25 19:1, Marc 3:8 10:1, Jean 1:28 3:26 10:40; τ. χειμάρρου τ. Κέδρων, Jean 18:1; 
__(b) τὸ π., the region beyond, the other side: Matthieu 8:18, 28 14:22 16:5, Marc 4:35 5:21 6:45 8:13; τ. θαλάσσης, Marc 5:1; τ. λίμνης, Luc 8:22.†

G4009.def:
πέρας, -ατος, τό
(πέρα, beyond), [in LXX chiefly for קֵץ, קָצָה and cognate forms ;] 
an end, limit, boundary; 
__(a) of space: chiefly in pl., τὰ π. τ. γῆς, Matthieu 12:42, Luc 11:31; τ. οἰκουμένης, Romains 10:18 (LXX); 
__(b) (opposite to ἀρχή) the end: with genitive, ἀντιλογίας, Hébreux 6:10.†

G4016.def:
περι-βάλλω 
[in LXX chiefly for כָּסָה pi., also for לָבַשׁ, עָטָה, etc. ;] 
to throw around or over, put on or over; 
__(a) of siege or defen­sive works: χάρακά σοι, Luc 19:43 (WH, mg.; παρεμβ-, WH, txt.); 
__(b) of clothing, to put on, wrap about, clothe with: with accusative of thing(s), Luc 23:11; with accusative of person(s), Matthieu 25:36, 38 25:43; with dupl. accusative (not cl.; Bl., § 34, 4), Jean 19:2; pf. pass., to have wrapped round one: with accusative of thing(s) (cl.), Marc 14:51 16:5, Apocalypse 7:9, 13 10:1 11:3 12:1 17:4 18:16 19:13; with dative of thing(s), Apocalypse 4:4 (WH, txt.; before ἐν, WH, mg.); fut., before ἐν (of. Deutéronome 22:12, Psaumes 45:9, 13), Apocalypse 3:5. Mid., to clothe oneself, wrap round or put on oneself: absol., Matthieu 6:29, Luc 12:27, Apocalypse 3:18; with accusative of thing(s), Matthieu 6:31, Actes 12:8, Apocalypse 19:8.†

G4061.def:
περι-τομή, -ῆς, ἡ
(περιτέμνω), [in LXX: Genèse 17:13, Exode 4:25-26 (מוּל ni., מוּלָה), Jérémie 11:16 * ;] 
circumcision; 
__(a) of the rite itself : Jean 7:22-23 Actes 7:8, Romains 4:11, Galates 5:11, Philippiens 3:5; 
__(b) of the state of circumcision: Romains 2:25-28 3:1, 1 Corinthiens 7:19, Galates 5:6 6:15, Colossiens 3:11; ἐν π. ὤν, Romains 4:10; 
__(with) by meton., π. = οἱ περιτμηθέντες, the circumcised: Romains 3:30 4:9, 12 15:8, Galates 2:7-9, Éphésiens 2:11; οἱ ἐκ τῆς π., of Jews, Romains 4:12; of Jewish Christians, Actes 11:2, Galates 2:12, Tite 1:10; οἱ ἐκ π. πιστοί, Actes 10:45; οἱ ὄντες ἐκ π., Colossiens 4:11 Metaphorical, Romains 2:29, Colossiens 2:11, Philippiens 3:3.†

G4088.def:
πικρία, -ας, ἡ
(πικρός), [in LXX chiefly for מַר and cognate forms ;] 
bitterness; 
__(a) of taste (Arist., Jérémie 15:17, al.); 
__(b) metaphorically, of temper, character, etc.: Romains 3:14 (LXX), Éphésiens 4:31; ῥίζα πικρίας, Hébreux 12:15; χολὴ π., a malignant disposition, Actes 8:23.†

G4094.def:
πίναξ, -ακος, ὁ 
[in LXX: 4Ma.17:7 R * ;] 
prop., a board, plank; hence, of various at wooden articles; 
__(a) a tablet; 
__(b) a disc, a dish: Matthieu 14:8, 11, Marc 6:25, 28 Luc 11:39.†
